{"date":14690801,"place":"Middleham","person":"keeper","title":"Letters under watch","quote":"Your letters may leave the chamber after they have been read. Those are the conditions.","context":"Warwick holds Edward in custody. A captive king still has a voice.","choices":[{"k":"council","t":"Demand witnesses to every restriction","d":"Preserve a lawful record; accept delay."},{"k":"direct","t":"Issue orders despite the guards","d":"Assert kingship; risk an immediate confrontation."}],"history":"edgcote","mood":"court","documents":["watched-letters"],"events":[{"date":"August 1469 · Middleham","title":"A king within another man’s walls.","text":"The table is laid and the candles supplied. At the doorway a keeper decides who may enter. Your name can still command a kingdom, but your letters must first cross this room.","art":"assets/art/transitions/middleham-confinement.webp","artAlt":"Edward at a writing table in a guarded chamber at Middleham.","mood":"instability"}]},
{"date":14690813,"place":"Middleham","person":"messenger","title":"The queen’s father","quote":"They have killed Rivers and young John. No hearing, no word from you. The queen is asking whether you knew.","context":"Anthony now inherits the Rivers title. Elizabeth has lost a father and a brother.","choices":[{"k":"queen","t":"Send word that the queen has your full protection","d":"Stand with the bereaved; deepen the quarrel."},{"k":"investigate","t":"Demand the names of those who ordered it","d":"Preserve evidence; postpone retaliation."}],"history":"rivers","mood":"reflection"},
{"date":14690820,"place":"Middleham","person":"jacquetta","title":"An accusation of witchcraft","quote":"They have killed my husband. Now they would make my daughter’s marriage a work of sorcery.","context":"A charge against Jacquetta can be used against Elizabeth’s legitimacy.","choices":[{"k":"investigate","t":"Require witnesses and a formal hearing","d":"Protect her through process; prolong the ordeal."},{"k":"queen","t":"Reject the accusation in your own name","d":"Defend the household; let enemies allege favouritism."}],"history":"jacquetta","mood":"court"},
{"date":14690901,"place":"Middleham","person":"hastings","title":"A message through the guard","quote":"They still come when they hear your name. But, Edward, they ask if you are coming back—or if we have left them to hope alone.","context":"Hastings can carry instructions to loyal households.","choices":[{"k":"hastings","t":"Ask him to gather reliable captains","d":"Build a way out; bind yourself to their service."},{"k":"faith","t":"Ask churchmen to mediate your release","d":"Seek a witnessed peace; share the credit."},{"k":"bounded","t":"Use Hastings’s captains to secure a route out","d":"Call on the following you helped create; owe them your freedom.","requires":{"stat":"hastings","min":25}}],"history":null,"mood":"court"},
{"date":14690901,"place":"Middleham","person":"clerk","title":"Writs no one obeys","quote":"The shires ask whose seal commands them. Your captors cannot make every household act.","context":"Holding the king does not make governing easy.","choices":[{"k":"direct","t":"Order the sheriffs to answer only to Edward","d":"Assert your indispensability; test their courage."},{"k":"settle","t":"Offer lawful commissions after your release","d":"Buy cooperation; promise future influence."}],"history":null,"mood":"court"},
{"date":14690901,"place":"Middleham","person":"bourchier","title":"A peace with witnesses","quote":"A free king must be able to speak without asking leave. Put that in the terms, or this peace is only a prettier prison.","context":"A settlement needs men willing to enforce it.","choices":[{"k":"council","t":"Record limits before the leading lords","d":"Make the peace visible; bind your own freedom."},{"k":"bounded","t":"Agree only to a temporary truce","d":"Keep options; leave grievances unresolved."}],"history":null,"mood":"court"},
{"date":14690901,"place":"Middleham","person":"captain","title":"A loose watch","quote":"A guard drinks with men who owe Warwick more than they owe you. He has offered to leave a door unbarred.","context":"Trusting an untested escape could put your life in an enemy’s hands.","choices":[{"k":"investigate","t":"Verify the offer through Hastings","d":"Reduce danger; lose the immediate opening."},{"k":"plot","t":"Trust the offer without a second witness","d":"Risk the king’s life for a chance at freedom."}],"history":null,"mood":"instability"},
{"date":14690901,"place":"Middleham","person":"elizabeth","title":"A letter from the queen","quote":"Come back with a crown you can still wear. I will not ask you to avenge us before you are free.","context":"A private bond asks something different from a public feud.","choices":[{"k":"settle","t":"Promise a measured return","d":"Preserve room for peace; defer vengeance."},{"k":"queen","t":"Promise that her household will be restored","d":"Give reassurance; commit future favour."}],"history":null,"mood":"intimacy","documents":["queen-middleham"]},
{"date":14690901,"place":"Middleham","person":"hastings","title":"The crown under guard","quote":"Warwick will bargain for your crown. I am trying to keep you alive, sire. Those are not always the same bargain.","context":"You can negotiate release without yielding the throne.","choices":[{"k":"settle","t":"Accept a witnessed settlement and retain the crown","d":"Regain freedom; carry unresolved grievances into the next year."},{"k":"depose","t":"Yield the crown under safe conduct","d":"Live in withdrawal; end Edward’s reign."},{"k":"escape","t":"Break out with the household guard","d":"Gamble your life; a weakened household may fail."}],"history":"edgcote","mood":"instability"}
