{"date":14701015,"place":"Low Countries","person":"hastings","title":"A borrowed chamber","quote":"We have a roof tonight. Tomorrow we must pay the men who crossed with you.","context":"Warwick has restored Henry VI. Edward’s household is now in exile.","choices":[{"k":"pay","t":"Spend the remaining plate on wages","d":"Keep the companions; diminish the reserve."},{"k":"promise","t":"Promise payment after the return","d":"Preserve resources; ask loyalty to bear another debt."}],"history":"readeption","mood":"reflection"},
{"date":14701015,"place":"Low Countries","person":"gloucester","title":"A brother beside you","quote":"I came with you. Give me work that makes the crossing mean something.","context":"Richard is eighteen, a companion in exile rather than a northern ruler.","choices":[{"k":"gloucester","t":"Ask Richard to prepare the fighting men","d":"Trust your brother; enlarge his standing."},{"k":"bounded","t":"Give him a limited command under your eye","d":"Train his judgment; curb his independence."}],"history":null,"mood":"court"},
{"date":14701015,"place":"Low Countries · by letter","person":"margaretYork","title":"Your sister’s influence","quote":"Charles has reasons to fear France. He also has reasons not to recognise your defeat. Let me find the language he will hear.","context":"Margaret of York is Duchess of Burgundy; her husband controls the aid.","choices":[{"k":"burgundy","t":"Let Margaret approach the duke privately","d":"Use a family bond; incur a personal debt."},{"k":"direct","t":"Send a formal request as King of England","d":"Preserve dignity; make refusal easier."}],"history":"burgundy","mood":"intimacy","documents":["sister-burgundy"],"courtPlace":"Low Countries"},
{"date":14701015,"place":"Low Countries · by letter","person":"elizabeth","title":"Behind sanctuary walls","quote":"We are safe while the abbey’s protection holds. Do not mistake safety for certainty.","context":"Elizabeth and her daughters have claimed sanctuary at Westminster.","choices":[{"k":"queen","t":"Send money and a trusted messenger","d":"Protect your family; spend exile funds."},{"k":"faith","t":"Ask the abbot to witness their protection","d":"Strengthen sanctuary; depend on the Church."}],"history":"sanctuary","mood":"intimacy","documents":["sanctuary-letter"],"courtPlace":"Low Countries"},
{"date":14701015,"place":"Low Countries","person":"envoy","title":"An inconvenient guest","quote":"The duke can tolerate you here more easily than he can openly arm you.","context":"Burgundian policy answers to its own dangers.","choices":[{"k":"burgundy","t":"Seek private credit through merchants","d":"Make quiet progress; accept future obligations."},{"k":"defer","t":"Wait for a formal promise","d":"Avoid uncertain terms; lose the season."}],"history":null,"mood":"court"},
{"date":14701015,"place":"Low Countries","person":"merchant","title":"Credit without a kingdom","quote":"What security does an exiled king offer? Your friends’ names may be worth more than your seal.","context":"Royal authority has become a claim upon future events.","choices":[{"k":"promise","t":"Pledge repayment from recovered customs","d":"Raise means; mortgage a possible restoration."},{"k":"pay","t":"Sell the remaining valuables","d":"Avoid another promise; reduce personal reserves."},{"k":"hastings","t":"Ask Hastings to bring trusted guarantors","d":"Raise credit through personal loyalty; deepen his claim."}],"history":null,"mood":"court"},
{"date":14701015,"place":"Low Countries","person":"hastings","title":"Letters to the shires","quote":"I can bring men south for you. They will come on my word—but I cannot ask them to risk everything for a rumour.","context":"Your former household still reaches across the Channel.","choices":[{"k":"hastings","t":"Let Hastings contact his affinity","d":"Use trusted ties; owe the return to his men."},{"k":"bounded","t":"Send several independent messengers","d":"Spread the risk; complicate the plan."}],"history":null,"mood":"court"},
{"date":14701103,"place":"Low Countries","person":"messenger","title":"A son in sanctuary","quote":"The queen has borne a son. He has been named Edward.","context":"The future Edward V was born on 2 November 1470 within Westminster sanctuary.","choices":[{"k":"queen","t":"Send thanks and provision to the queen","d":"Affirm the family; divert scarce resources."},{"k":"faith","t":"Have prayers offered for mother and child","d":"Give the birth public meaning; expose your hopes."},{"k":"direct","t":"Announce the birth to your supporters in England","d":"Give the cause a future; expose your hopes to enemies."}],"history":"prince","mood":"intimacy"},
{"date":14701104,"place":"Low Countries","person":"clerk","title":"Henry’s government","quote":"The restored king’s council calls you a usurper. Men who served you are seeking pardons.","context":"Warwick governs in Henry VI’s name. Those men are not your councillors.","choices":[{"k":"pardon","t":"Promise mercy to those who return to you","d":"Keep a path open; forgive opportunism."},{"k":"assert","t":"Warn that betrayal will cost them office","d":"Deter desertion; make return more dangerous."}],"history":"readeption","mood":"court","documents":["chronicle-leaf"]},
{"date":14701105,"place":"Low Countries","person":"gloucester","title":"A small force","quote":"We cannot take an army equal to every lord in England. We must land where one friend can become several.","context":"The first days ashore may matter more than numbers at sea.","choices":[{"k":"bounded","t":"Prepare a small, disciplined landing force","d":"Control the risk; accept limited strength."},{"k":"mobilize","t":"Spend more on soldiers","d":"Improve the landing; deepen the cost."}],"history":null,"mood":"campaign"},
{"date":14701201,"place":"Low Countries","person":"chaplain","title":"The king without a chapel","quote":"A borrowed room can still hold a prayer. Your men would like to hear you join them.","context":"Faith binds a household when its outward splendour is gone.","choices":[{"k":"faith","t":"Keep a common service with the companions","d":"Share their uncertainty; set command aside for a moment."},{"k":"direct","t":"Use the gathering to announce the return","d":"Give resolve a voice; turn worship into politics."}],"history":null,"mood":"reflection"},
{"date":14710101,"place":"Aire","person":"envoy","title":"Aid with a price","quote":"Burgundy has reason to help you now. It will remember that help when you possess England again.","context":"The chance to return also creates the debts of a restored reign.","choices":[{"k":"burgundy","t":"Accept the duke’s assistance","d":"Obtain ships and money; owe future consideration."},{"k":"bounded","t":"Limit the undertaking in writing","d":"Protect future freedom; ask for less aid."}],"history":null,"mood":"court","documents":["burgundian-memorial"]},
{"date":14710101,"place":"Aire","person":"hastings","title":"Clarence’s unease","quote":"Henry’s restoration has not made your brother its heir. He may be willing to listen.","context":"A reconciliation would weaken Warwick’s coalition.","choices":[{"k":"settle","t":"Offer Clarence a private way back","d":"Recover a brother; alarm those he betrayed."},{"k":"assert","t":"Require him to make the first submission","d":"Defend your dignity; risk losing the opening."},{"k":"burgundy","t":"Let Margaret carry the offer to Clarence","d":"Use a sister’s influence; leave the terms partly in her hands."}],"history":null,"mood":"court"},
{"date":14710201,"place":"Low Countries","person":"captain","title":"The ships are ready","quote":"We can cross with the first fair wind. Stores sufficient for a longer wait will cost us more.","context":"The sea does not answer to a royal timetable.","choices":[{"k":"hold","t":"Wait for sound sailing weather","d":"Protect the force; pay for the delay."},{"k":"pursue","t":"Sail at the first usable opening","d":"Keep momentum; accept the greater danger."}],"history":null,"mood":"campaign"},
{"date":14710314,"place":"Ravenspur","person":"hastings","title":"England underfoot","quote":"Tell them you seek your duchy first. Let them discover that the king has returned after they have opened the gates.","context":"Edward landed at Ravenspur in March 1471.","choices":[{"k":"bounded","t":"Advance under the claim to your duchy","d":"Reduce resistance; leave your full intention unstated."},{"k":"direct","t":"Declare your royal title immediately","d":"Assert the crown; provoke its enemies."}],"history":"return","mood":"campaign","events":[{"date":"14 March 1471 · Ravenspur","title":"The shore beneath your feet.","text":"You have come back with a small force. The first men you meet look at your companions before they answer you. England is before you; its obedience is still to be won.","art":"assets/art/transitions/return-england.webp","artAlt":"Edward and a small company disembark on an uncertain English shore.","mood":"campaign"}]},
{"date":14710320,"place":"York","person":"sheriff","title":"The gates of York","quote":"The city asks that your men pass peacefully and pay for what they take.","context":"A welcoming gate can close behind an undisciplined force.","choices":[{"k":"pay","t":"Guarantee payment and strict discipline","d":"Keep the city quiet; spend campaign means."},{"k":"oath","t":"Bind the captains publicly to good conduct","d":"Make honour a security; depend on obedience."}],"history":null,"mood":"court"},
{"date":14710325,"place":"Nottingham","person":"hastings","title":"The first reinforcements","quote":"These men have come because I asked. Let them hear why they should remain.","context":"Hastings’s affinity gives substance to the return.","choices":[{"k":"hastings","t":"Receive the captains through Hastings","d":"Reward the bond that brought them; strengthen his hand."},{"k":"direct","t":"Take their oaths personally","d":"Make service royal; claim their loyalty yourself."}],"history":null,"mood":"court"},
{"date":14710404,"place":"Coventry","person":"clarence","title":"A brother returns","quote":"I can bring my men across. I cannot undo where they stood before today.","context":"Clarence rejoins Edward in April 1471.","choices":[{"k":"settle","t":"Receive him under a witnessed reconciliation","d":"Recover his force; leave old hurts unresolved."},{"k":"bounded","t":"Accept his men but restrict his command","d":"Gain strength; keep distrust visible."}],"history":"return","mood":"intimacy"},
{"date":14710411,"place":"London","person":"elizabeth","title":"Out of sanctuary","quote":"Your son has never seen you. Come into the room before you return to the road.","context":"Elizabeth leaves sanctuary as Edward regains London; Warwick’s army remains in the field.","choices":[{"k":"queen","t":"Give the household a night together","d":"Renew the bond; postpone military business."},{"k":"mobilize","t":"See them briefly, then prepare the army","d":"Protect the return; let duty consume the reunion."}],"history":"sanctuary","mood":"intimacy"},
{"date":14710522,"place":"Westminster","person":"hastings","title":"The crown regained","quote":"The men who followed Warwick ask whether your peace has a place for them. Those who stayed with you are waiting for their reward.","context":"Barnet and Tewkesbury have restored your crown. Henry VI is dead. Your enemies’ households and your own promises remain.","history":"barnet","mood":"reflection","choices":[{"k":"pardon","t":"Receive former followers under new oaths","d":"Rebuild obedience; leave old networks alive."},{"k":"assert","t":"Reserve office for those who stood with you","d":"Reward loyalty; leave powerful men excluded."},{"k":"council","t":"Have the terms witnessed across the households","d":"Broaden acceptance; bind your own freedom."}],"events":[{"date":"14 April 1471 · Barnet","title":"The kingmaker falls.","text":"In the mist outside Barnet, Edward defeats Warwick’s army. Warwick is killed. The man whose service helped make your crown can no longer answer for the people who followed him.","history":"barnet"},{"date":"4 May 1471 · Tewkesbury","title":"A cause loses its heir.","text":"Margaret of Anjou’s army is defeated. Her son, Edward of Westminster, dies. The battlefield has decided who holds the crown. It has not settled how the surviving households will live beneath it.","history":"tewkesbury"}]}
